ays that he struggles to convey it  verbally because it has never been  conveyed to him or by him verbally it  all just developed due to this repeated  exposure to murder via these videotapes  in increasingly brutal and creative ways  to the point where killing itself has  become practically Dane I do think we  still have at least one more step before  we understand the motive of the curta  massacre currently all I can think of is  that their killing was essential to  build the reputation of meteor city as a  criminal Haven where anything goes  because hey it's pretty difficult to  commit a crime larger than genocide plus  there's also the whole aspect of body  part collecting which probably does have  a bit of a crossover with the um I guess  let's call it the film industry and I  would personally find that answer  satisfying because it doesn't vindicate  or even attempt to vindicate their  actions Sheila is a very interesting  aspect of this chapter because she is  shown departing the group both  physically and metaphorically which  gives us two options for her either  she's feeling very guilty because she  was somehow involved in this dark  industry or Sheila has become  disillusioned by her friends who all  seem to be very quick to just throw  their lives away to become villains and  remembering that Sheila's dream is to  become a hunter she may have been the  only real person to escape this  friendship group with any real hope  remaining which then resulted in her  unintentionally saving karapika but that  in turn ended up killing Sheila's  friends over again and so we've got some  very Shakespearean style tragedy  Happening Here an unexpected highlight  of the chapter was further development  of the crolo over again relationship  this is something I definitely did not  expect but when UVA refused leadership  of the troop and instead nominated  crawler that absolutely generated some  feels a very mixed mess of feelings that  is because it is quite touching these  two have had their moment of  understanding but also knowing what it  leads to just completely twists and  subverts the sweet nature of it I tell  you what though this makes crolo's  Requiem for over again so so so much  sadder in retrospect I mean when I was  going through York new city for the  first time I saw that as an act of pure  respect for his Fallen comrade like the  Phantom troops equivalent of a funeral  but now I almost see it as pure mourning  like a raw emotional release of grief in  this case taken out in extremely violent  ways but still I suppose my question at  this point is whether or not the troop  have actually found sarasa's Killers yet  because if not I imagine that this would  need to tie into the succession more  events however they very much could have  dealt with sarasa's Killers years and  years and years ago because here's the  thing chrolo and cropicus stories are  now basically the same a Vengeance Quest  where both Geniuses resolve to become a  villain for the sake of the fallen and I  can see a situation where crolo and the  troop did find sarasa's Killers then  they viciously kill murdered them and  acted you know the Vengeance but then  ended up in the exact same spot that  karapika did after killing uvgin that  sense of emptiness and a kind of sadness  that achieving Revenge did absolutely  nothing but then I also thought back to  York New Again specifically the moment  where parkinoda asked gone in kilua why  they won't run away and they answer that  it's because they're krapika's friends  and they don't want him to become a  murderer AKA they don't want him to walk  down the same path that crolo and the  troop did now gone obviously didn't know  that but paku noticed saw the  similarities and that's why she was  thankful because karapika unlike them  had friends that were willing to stop  them doing what they did after Sarasota  I mean sort of krapika did still kill  uvgin but hence why Finks and feitan  also treated gone and killua much more  empathetically at the auction because  parkunoda included that memory to give  them which is particularly striking  because gone and kilowatt are obviously  children and pretty much smack bang on  the same age as most of the troop were  when sarasa died these last few chapters  have recontextualized so much of the  series and after we finished here I  desperately want to reread all of York  new city with this new context in mind  speaking of parkinot's powers though  she's one of the troop members whose  abilities make a tragic degree of sense  hakunoda can read memories and I imagine  that that was designed so that she could  ultimately read and confirm exactly who  it was that killed sarasu and she's  definitely not the only one impacted by  this Marchi is another tragic example  her string Powers were formed out of a  desire to make sure that nobody ended up  like sarasa chopped into pieces and such  and now machi's whole thing is about  putting people back together so Machi  very much took after the ninen bomber  whose name is renko and looks really  cool actually she seems a bit more  overly designed than your usual tagashi  character and I'm hoping that means that  we'll see more of her in the future also  Machi could just naturally see Aura I  mean obviously not naturally it would  have had to be awakened somehow but  that's kind of crazy because even after  Awakening you would generally need to  use guillot to actually see raura Machi  did not unless she was unconsciously  using gear in which case she is an  absolute genius Machi is a very special  nen user and she's also being quite  isolated in this flashback generally  operating counter to everyone else so  getting her in little slivers of  individual Focus very much like how  she's currently on her own now aboard  the Blackwell one back to abilities  though crolo skill Hunter is very much  because he prioritizes a wide breadth of  information and tools to use for his  plan but even feitan's pain Packer could  be a direct result of sarasa that innate  desire to inflict as much damage as was  done to her onto sarasa's Killers  because that's basically what pain  Packer does it takes every bit of damage  that you've done and makes you pay for  it with interest but you know the one  key question that we still have an  answer in this flashback is who was the  original number eight and number four  members of the truth because we now know  that whoever they were they definitely  weren't part of the founding members so  those two must have been collected  afterwards and if this troop flashback  does continue I would love to see it  cover who those two members were as well  as briefly touch on the recruitment  origin of members like banolanov shizuku  and kotope because they feel like as  soon as we reach that point then the  troop storyline is ready to be wrapped  up in a neat little package meaning that  we can prepare for most if not all of  them today but also thinking back on it  during the best time of crolo's life  without initial cleanup ranges episode  he was most animated and arguably best  at playing the villain so it's no  surprise that he's done such a great job  of that as an adult as well and also not  to be neglected there is a much grander  irony to the situation because as a  result of crolo setting up his spiderweb  of meteor city as a Nexus of human evil  that is exactly what has attracted gyro  there our living incarnation of evil and  with all of the troop currently out of  the picture there is nothing whatsoever  stopping jira from using the evil that  crolo has built and overseen as the  first step in the ultimate destruction  of humanity

